> associator i, j, k
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator i, i, j
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -j - (-j) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator 1, i, j
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = k - (k) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator 0.1+i, 0.2+j, 0.3+k
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -497/500 + 4i/25 - 17j/100 + 8k/25 - (-497/500 + 4i/25 - 17j/100 + 8k/25) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator e1, e2, e4
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
> associator e2, e4, e1
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
> associator e1, e1, e2
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -e2 - (-e2) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the octonions)
> associator 1, e1, e2
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e3 - (e3) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the octonions)
> associator e1+e2, e3+e4, e5+e6
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -2 - 2 e7 - (-2 + 2 e7) = -4 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
> associator e1, e8, e9
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the sedenions)
> associator e16, e17, e18
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -e19 - (e19) = -2 e19
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the cd(32) numbers)
> associator e1, e16, e17
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the cd(32) numbers)
> commutator i, j
[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k
  they do not commute
> commutator j, i
[a, b] = ab - ba = -k - (k) = -2k
  they do not commute
> commutator i, i
[a, b] = ab - ba = -1 - (-1) = 0
  they commute
> commutator 1, i
[a, b] = ab - ba = i - (i) = 0
  they commute
> commutator e1, e2
[a, b] = ab - ba = e3 - (-e3) = 2 e3
  they do not commute
> commutator e2, e1
[a, b] = ab - ba = -e3 - (e3) = -2 e3
  they do not commute
> commutator e30, e31
[a, b] = ab - ba = -e1 - (e1) = -2 e1
  they do not commute
> commutator (e1+e2), (e3+e4)
[a, b] = ab - ba = e1 - e2 + e5 + e6 - (-e1 + e2 - e5 - e6) = 2 e1 - 2 e2 + 2 e5 + 2 e6
  they do not commute
